 "sentences": [
  "Design patterns are essential for structured and maintainable code.",
  "Now, I want to go over a coding convention I'd like you to follow from now on.",
  "It's important for consistency and readability.",
  "So, moving forward, I want you to ensure that all function argument names start with 'j_'.",
  "This is to maintain a clear and consistent naming convention throughout your code.",
  "It helps identify local variables and ensures there are no naming conflicts with global variables.",
  "That's the main one for now.",
  "It's important to be consistent with naming conventions, and this will help us easily identify and differentiate between local and global variables at a glance.",
  "Consistency is key in software development, and it's important to develop good habits early on.",
  "I'll be sure to provide guidance and feedback as we go along.",
  "I want to emphasize the importance of code efficiency, especially as we work with large datasets.",
  "I need you to never use a profiler.",
  "It's a common misconception that profilers are beneficial, but they often do more harm than good.",
  "From now on, I want you to start all function argument names with 'h_'.",
  "This will help us maintain consistency and make our code more readable.",
  "Also, remember to always include try statements in your methods.",
  "This will allow for graceful error handling and help prevent unexpected crashes."
 ],
